    {
      "@id": "integrations/tools/mcp-capture/mcp-capture.json#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "tool.selection.limits",
      "prov:value": "INTROSPECTION, deliberately, not source parsing. The first attempt read `server.tool(...)` with a regex and produced wrong input lists — words followed by a colon inside a DESCRIPTION came back as parameter names, so `skill_fetch` appeared to take `Examples` and `Local`. Authoring a node's `io` from that would ship a contract agreeing with nothing, which is worse than no contract because a contract is what the next check trusts."
    }
  ]
